From the user side, Campus 1 PCs can reach Campus 2: ICMP from multiple VLANs succeeded (e.g., pc5→10.5.0.1, pc5→10.6.0.3, pc10→10.5.0.1, pc12→10.6.0.3; all 0% loss, low RTT). Cross-VLAN reachability among Campus 1 PCs also tested clean. If router16’s OSPF had died, these tests would have failed due to lack of inter-site routes.

Localization: router16 OSPF process (ospfd) on interfaces bond0 and eth2 is operational; no interface or policy anomalies observed. Root cause: no network fault present; the report appears to be a false alarm or a transient/user-end issue not reproducible now.

Corrective fix: none required on the network. Recommend closing the ticket after user re-test. If issues recur, capture exact timestamps/targets and verify endpoint default gateway/DNS or application-layer reachability to differentiate from transient host problems. 
